  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"1.5.7\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pzstd\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/facebook/zstd/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 37d7284556b20954e56e1ca85b80226768902e2edabd3b649e9e72c0c9012ee3\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - win\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - make\n  host:\n    # pzstd uses the static-only zstd API and compiles against the headers in this\n    # source tree, so it links the libzstd.a of the exact same release\n    - zstd-static ${{ version }}.*\n  ignore_run_exports:\n    by_name:\n      - zstd\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - pzstd\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - zstd\n    script:\n      - pzstd --version\n      - echo \"hello pzstd\" > input.txt\n      - pzstd -q -p 2 input.txt -o input.txt.zst\n      - test \"$(pzstd -q -dc input.txt.zst)\" = \"hello pzstd\"\n      - test \"$(zstd -q -dc input.txt.zst)\" = \"hello pzstd\"\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://facebook.github.io/zstd/\n  summary: Parallel Zstandard compression and decompression tool\n  description: |\n    pzstd is a parallel implementation of the Zstandard command line tool. It\n    splits the input into independent frames that are compressed and\n    decompressed on multiple threads, and its output can be read by the regular\n    zstd tool.\n  license: BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0-only\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - COPYING\n  repository: https://github.com/facebook/zstd\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - baszalmstra\n",
